      message: "No background noise, no big speech - just that split second your expression completely shifted when you realized I was standing there.\n\nI never needed an excuse to show up; just seeing your face in the middle of a regular day was worth every mile.\n\n The days leading up to this moment were some of the heaviest days we ever had to endure. It took a real, painful toll on both of us, and there were moments when everything felt completely overwhelming. But the universe simply refused to let that hurdle tear us apart. It showed us that no obstacle was bigger than what we have; instead of breaking us, it stripped everything away until only pure honesty was left. We came out on the other side believing in each other more than we ever had before, trusting each other deeper, and realizing that we were going to be unbreakable. This day, June 20th, was our quiet, beautiful fresh start. To pull this off at an all-women’s college took an entire undercover operation. I rolled up to your campus security gate and spun an elaborate tale on the spot, telling the guards I was there to inquire about admission for my sister Dee who lives in the UK. Miraculously, they bought it, handed me a campus pass, and I drove right in. I parked the car and walked straight to your canteen, my heart pounding with nervous excitement, trying to reach out to Chinnu to coordinate. The moment I found out Chinnu hadn't come to college that day, I panicked for a second - until I told her I was standing right there on your campus to surprise you. She understood the assignment instantly. She concocted the whole story about her lab records being with someone who was leaving for their village, convincing you that you had to rush down to the canteen the exact second your lunch break started to collect them. I waited at that canteen for almost an hour, watching the clock tick down, just waiting for the bell to ring. And the second you walked into sight, I pulled out my phone and hit record. You looked around, saw me standing right there in the middle of your college, and the pure shock on your face was priceless. You never saw it coming. The video didn’t capture any audio - it saved completely silent - but the silence says everything. You don’t need sound to see the genuine shock melting into those smiles and giggles, or the disbelief written all over your face. We sneaked back to the car to share your lunch together in private, talking about everything, sharing a quiet kiss before you had to head back to class. That single lunch break set off something special - a tradition of us stealing moments together over the next two and a half months whenever we could manage it. Looking back from across the distance now, this day is my constant reminder: no matter how hard things get, we always find our way back to each other, and we always find a way to make each other smile.\n\n",
