      subtitle: "25 June",
      message: "By this point, the campus security guards didn't even need my undercover stories anymore - I'm pretty sure they just recognized my face and thought, 'Yep, that guy is back again.' But the mission this afternoon wasn't just to see you; it was urgent. You had been skipping lunch and throwing your food away lately, and the thought of you starving yourself in the middle of a long day was driving me crazy. So I decided right then that if you wouldn't eat on your own, I was coming down there to make sure you did. I drove forty minutes through the scorching Hyderabad heat. To make sure Dad wouldn't notice the petrol needle dropping faster than usual, I made the executive decision to suffer through the entire drive without turning on the AC. Not a single drop of cool air. I wanted to save every ounce of fuel so that the moment you opened the car door, I could blast the air conditioning and let you escape the brutal sun into pure cold comfort. I sat parked in that car baking for at least twenty minutes. It got so hot I was practically seeing blurry double visions through the windshield - until suddenly, like an actual ray of hope, I spotted you walking toward the car. And of course, in classic universe fashion: the first time I sneaked in looking homeless, half the campus managed to spot me; today, when I actually put effort into getting dressed up just to see you, not a single soul was around to witness it. You came in swearing you were in no mood to eat lunch at all. But within minutes, there we were in the front seats with your lunchbox and two hot packets of Manchuria. Just thinking about it makes my mouth water. Every single bite of home lunch had to be paired with a piece of Manchuria - I fed you, you fed me, back and forth until neither of us could stop smiling. Forty minutes in the heat and sweat melted away the second we shared that meal together.",
